      "content": "the sweden/norway examples are a bit dated tho right? i've read that most of those countries actually ended up repealing theirs because they caused too much capital flight. wouldn't you say the risk of driving away the very people who fund the economy is a much more certain outcome than the theoretical benefit of reducing inequality?",
